<title>USA: W.Va. $99 mln repriced, top yield cut to 5.50 pct.</title>
<headline>W.Va. $99 mln repriced, top yield cut to 5.50 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>PaineWebber Inc said Wednesday it repriced State Building Commission of West Virginia's $99.96 million lottery bond deal, lowering yields five basis points in several maturities and cutting the top yield in 2010 to 5.50 percent from 5.55 percent.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:</p>
<p>THE STATE BUILDING COMMISSION OF WEST VIRGINIA</p>
<p>RE: $98,960,000*</p>
<p>LOTTERY REVENUE BONDS, 1997 SERIES A</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD.</p>
<p>MOODY'S: Aaa		 S&amp;P: AAA		 FITCH: AAA</p>
<p>	  UNDERLYING:Baa	 UNDERLYING:BBB-  UNDERLYING:BBB+</p>
<p>MBIA INSURED</p>
<p>DATED: 01/01/1997	  FIRST COUPON: 07/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 07/01</p>
<p> MATURITY		AMOUNT*    COUPON	   PRICE</p>
<p>07/01/1997		7,405M    5.00  %	  NRO</p>
<p>07/01/1998		5,185M    5.00  %	  NRO</p>
<p>07/01/1999		5,440M    5.50  %	  4.30</p>
<p>07/01/2000		5,740M    5.50  %	  4.50</p>
<p>07/01/2001		6,055M    5.00  %	  4.65</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>07/01/2002		6,360M    5.00  %	  4.75</p>
<p>07/01/2003		6,680M    5.00  %	  4.85</p>
<p>07/01/2004		7,010M    5.00  %	  4.95</p>
<p>07/01/2005		7,360M    5.50  %	  5.00</p>
<p>07/01/2006		7,765M    5.50  %	  5.10</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>07/01/2007		8,195M    5.50  %	  5.20</p>
<p>07/01/2008		8,645M    5.25  %	  5.30</p>
<p>07/01/2009		9,100M    5.25  %	  5.40</p>
<p>07/01/2010		8,020M    5.25  %	  5.50</p>
<p>CALL FEATURES: 07/01/2007    102.00</p>
<p>		   DTP 07/01/2009</p>
<p>* - APPROXIMATE SUBJECT TO CHANGE</p>
<p>The compliance addendum MSRB Rule G-11 will apply.</p>
<p>The bonds will be blue skyed in all states.</p>
<p>The award is expected Thursday, January 9, 1997.</p>
<p>Delivery is expected on January 30, 1997.</p>
<p>This issue is book entry through DTC.</p>
<p>PaineWebber Incorporated</p>
<p>Ferris, Baker Watts Inc.</p>
<p>Wheat First Butcher Singer</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
